  "functions": {
    "get": {
      "description": "Fetches an OCI image or index from a registry and returns detailed information about it, including the manifest, configuration, and platform-specific images.\n\nThe function accepts either a tag or digest reference and returns an object with the following properties:\n\n- `full_ref` - The complete reference with digest (e.g., `cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base@sha256:abcd1234...`)\n- `digest` - The digest of the image or index (e.g., `sha256:abcd1234...`)\n- `tag` - The tag if one was provided in the input (e.g., `latest`)\n- `manifest` - The OCI manifest object containing:\n  - `schema_version` - The manifest schema version\n  - `media_type` - The media type of the manifest\n  - `config` - The config descriptor (for images)\n  - `layers` - List of layer descriptors (for images)\n  - `annotations` - Key-value annotations\n  - `manifests` - List of manifest descriptors (for indexes)\n  - `subject` - Subject descriptor (for referrers)\n- `images` - Map of platform strings to image objects (populated for multi-arch indexes). Each image contains:\n  - `digest` - The platform-specific image digest\n  - `image_ref` - The full reference for the platform-specific image\n- `config` - The image configuration (populated for single-arch images only). Contains:\n  - `env` - List of environment variables\n  - `user` - The user to run as\n  - `working_dir` - The working directory\n  - `entrypoint` - The entrypoint command\n  - `cmd` - The default command arguments\n  - `created_at` - Timestamp when the image was created\n\n**Note:** This function makes a network request to the registry to fetch the image metadata. Authentication is handled via the default keychain (Docker config, credential helpers, etc.).\n\n## Example: Single-arch image\n\n```terraform\noutput \"image_info\" {\n  value = provider::oci::get(\"cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base:latest\")\n}\n```\n\n## Example: Multi-arch index\n\n```terraform\nlocals {\n  multi_arch = provider::oci::get(\"cgr.dev/chainguard/static:latest\")\n}\n\noutput \"linux_amd64\" {\n  value = local.multi_arch.images[\"linux/amd64\"]\n}\n```\n\n## Example: Using the config\n\n```terraform\nlocals {\n  image = provider::oci::get(\"cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base:latest\")\n}\n\noutput \"entrypoint\" {\n  value = local.image.config.entrypoint\n}\n\noutput \"environment\" {\n  value = local.image.config.env\n}\n```",
      "summary": "Fetches an OCI image or index from a registry and returns detailed metadata.",
      "return_type": [
        "object",
        {
          "config": [
            "object",
            {
              "cmd": [
                "list",
                "string"
              ],
              "created_at": "string",
              "entrypoint": [
                "list",
                "string"
              ],
              "env": [
                "list",
                "string"
              ],
              "user": "string",
              "working_dir": "string"
            }
          ],
          "digest": "string",
          "full_ref": "string",
          "images": [
            "map",
            [
              "object",
              {
                "digest": "string",
                "image_ref": "string"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "manifest": [
            "object",
            {
              "annotations": [
                "map",
                "string"
              ],
              "config": [
                "object",
                {
                  "digest": "string",
                  "media_type": "string",
                  "platform": [
                    "object",
                    {
                      "architecture": "string",
                      "os": "string",
                      "os_version": "string",
                      "variant": "string"
                    }
                  ],
                  "size": "number"
                }
              ],
              "layers": [
                "list",
                [
                  "object",
                  {
                    "digest": "string",
                    "media_type": "string",
                    "platform": [
                      "object",
                      {
                        "architecture": "string",
                        "os": "string",
                        "os_version": "string",
                        "variant": "string"
                      }
                    ],
                    "size": "number"
                  }
                ]
              ],
              "manifests": [
                "list",
                [
                  "object",
                  {
                    "digest": "string",
                    "media_type": "string",
                    "platform": [
                      "object",
                      {
                        "architecture": "string",
                        "os": "string",
                        "os_version": "string",
                        "variant": "string"
                      }
                    ],
                    "size": "number"
                  }
                ]
              ],
              "media_type": "string",
              "schema_version": "number",
              "subject": [
                "object",
                {
                  "digest": "string",
                  "media_type": "string",
                  "platform": [
                    "object",
                    {
                      "architecture": "string",
                      "os": "string",
                      "os_version": "string",
                      "variant": "string"
                    }
                  ],
                  "size": "number"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "tag": "string"
        }
      ],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "input",
          "description": "The OCI reference string to get.",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ]
    },
    "parse": {
      "description": "Converts a fully qualified OCI image reference with a digest into an object representation with the following properties:\n\n- `registry` - The registry hostname (e.g., `cgr.dev`)\n- `repo` - The repository path without the registry (e.g., `chainguard/wolfi-base`)\n- `registry_repo` - The full registry and repository path (e.g., `cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base`)\n- `digest` - The digest identifier (e.g., `sha256:abcd1234...`)\n- `pseudo_tag` - A pseudo tag format combining unused with the digest (e.g., `unused@sha256:abcd1234...`)\n- `ref` - The complete reference string as provided\n\n**Note:** The input must include a digest. References with only a tag (without a digest) will result in an error.\n\n## Example\n\n```terraform\noutput \"parsed\" {\n  value = provider::oci::parse(\"cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base@sha256:abcd1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890ab\")\n}\n```\n\nThis returns:\n```json\n{\n  \"registry\": \"cgr.dev\",\n  \"repo\": \"chainguard/wolfi-base\",\n  \"registry_repo\": \"cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base\",\n  \"digest\": \"sha256:abcd1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890ab\",\n  \"pseudo_tag\": \"unused@sha256:abcd1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890ab\",\n  \"ref\": \"cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base@sha256:abcd1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890ab\"\n}\n```",
      "summary": "Parses a pinned OCI string into its constituent parts.",
      "return_type": [
        "object",
        {
          "digest": "string",
          "pseudo_tag": "string",
          "ref": "string",
          "registry": "string",
          "registry_repo": "string",
          "repo": "string"
        }
      ],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "input",
          "description": "The OCI reference string to parse.",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
